# AXIS-COMPLETENESS -- the callable-indirection matrix (post-Track-B3).
#
# Every cell of the three axes gets one call with a distinguishable output, so a
# partial regression trips MULTIPLE lines (Core #12). The axes are independent:
#   root                × callable-provenance × arg-spelling
#   plain-local | &-param   LOCAL | PARAM         `&`
# and the reference-grade shape at each cell is "write through the borrow".
#
# Under Track B3 (D31-uniform, ledger 2026-07-20 D31 ADDENDUM-2), the bare-arg
# cells (L2 = plain-local root + bare arg, G1 = &-param root + bare arg) are
# REJECTED at `gg check` with `E_OwnershipMismatch` -- the same rule direct
# calls have long enforced now applies uniformly to indirect calls. Those cells
# therefore no longer belong here (they cannot RUN); they are pinned as
# check-time REJECTS in the sibling NEG fixtures:
#   indirect_call_bare_arg_amp_callee_error.gg        (was L2)
#   indirect_call_bare_arg_param_amp_callee_error.gg  (was F2 / analogous shape)
#
# Pre-Track-B1 measurements (both backends):
#   L1 LOCAL callable + plain-local + &-arg     -> SEGV (was cell 1 of scout table)
#   P1 PARAM callable + plain-local + &-arg     -> SEGV (was cells 2, 4)
#   G2 PARAM callable + &-param    + &-arg      -> 101  (accidentally green same
#                                                        family; the sibling fixture
#                                                        `callable_ref_param_amp.gg`
#                                                        pins the analogous cell on
#                                                        a `Counter &` root)
#
# The output digits below identify which cell ran, so a regression that hits
# only one cell prints a still-recognisable-but-wrong sequence rather than
# silently degrading to the correct total. Cells L1/P1 formerly SEGV'd, so a
# regression that reintroduces the bug drops the line's second column (or
# crashes the run before it can print).
void bump(int &n):
    n = n + 100

void with_local_amp():
    int a = 1
    Callable[void(&int)] cb = bump
    cb(&a)
    print(f"L1={a}")

void with_param_amp(Callable[void(&int)] cb):
    int a = 3
    cb(&a)
    print(f"P1={a}")

void with_param_amp_ampparam(Callable[void(&int)] cb, int &a):
    cb(&a)
    print(f"G2={a}")

void main():
    with_local_amp()
    with_param_amp(bump)
    int g2 = 5
    with_param_amp_ampparam(bump, &g2)
